finalText:
**Fixed — all 625 tests pass now.**

`orderTotal` in `src/pricing.js` was computing tax on the pre-discount amount instead of the discounted one, even though the comment above it said tax should apply after the discount. Fixed it to charge tax on the discounted total:

```js
function orderTotal(cents, discountPct, taxRate) {
  const discounted = applyDiscount(cents, discountPct);
  return roundCents(discounted * (1 + taxRate));
}
```

Only rows with both a discount and a tax rate ever exposed the bug, which is why most cases passed.
